flowchart TD
    CALLER["caller enters do_unlinkat(dfd, name)<br/><b>state:</b> normal kernel call/args in registers"]
    PATCH["fentry patch site<br/><b>does:</b> architecture ftrace/BPF machinery replaces NOPs with an entry call path<br/><b>why next:</b> trampoline must run before the function body<br/><b>state:</b> original args are still available"]
    TRAMP["BPF trampoline<br/><b>does:</b> saves argument registers into the BPF calling convention<br/><b>why next:</b> verifier-approved BPF program expects typed args<br/><b>state:</b> ctx/typed args ready"]
    BPF["your fentry BPF program<br/><b>does:</b> observes dfd/name before unlink logic runs<br/><b>why next:</b> returns 0 to continue kernel execution<br/><b>state:</b> optional event data prepared"]
    RING["ringbuf submit<br/><b>does:</b> copies observation to userspace-visible buffer<br/><b>why next:</b> tracing side effect is complete"]
    RESTORE["trampoline epilogue<br/><b>does:</b> restores registers and returns to patched function entry<br/><b>state:</b> kernel can run as if tracing were transparent"]
    BODY["do_unlinkat body<br/><b>does:</b> path lookup, permission checks, unlink<br/><b>state:</b> real syscall behavior continues"]
    RET["return to caller"]

    CALLER --> PATCH --> TRAMP --> BPF --> RING --> RESTORE --> BODY --> RET

    classDef hot fill:#ffe5b4,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bpf fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    classDef kern fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#374151,stroke-width:1px
    class PATCH,TRAMP hot
    class BPF,RING bpf
    class CALLER,RESTORE,BODY,RET kern
